# Frontend Design & UX Rules

## Scope
This rule applies to all UI components, pages, and design-related code in `src/components/`, `src/pages/`, and `src/index.css`.

## Mobile-First Design Principles

### Responsive Breakpoints
- Always design mobile-first, then enhance for larger screens
- Use Tailwind breakpoints: `sm:` (640px), `md:` (768px), `lg:` (1024px)
- Mobile detection: Use `useIsMobile()` hook (768px breakpoint)
- Never use fixed widths on mobile - use `w-full` or percentage-based widths

### Mobile Carousel Pattern
When implementing carousels/swipers for mobile:

1. **Required Components**:
   - Use `embla-carousel-react` via `@/components/ui/carousel`
   - Import: `Carousel`, `CarouselContent`, `CarouselItem`, `CarouselApi`

2. **State Management**:
   ```tsx
   const [api, setApi] = useState<CarouselApi>();
   const [current, setCurrent] = useState(0);
   const [canScrollPrev, setCanScrollPrev] = useState(false);
   const [canScrollNext, setCanScrollNext] = useState(false);
   ```

3. **Configuration**:
   ```tsx
   opts={{
     align: "center",        // Center snap for peek effect
     loop: false,            // No infinite loop
     dragFree: false,        // Snap to slides
     containScroll: "trimSnaps",
   }}
   ```

4. **Peek Effect**:
   - Use `basis-[85%]` on `CarouselItem` to show 15% of adjacent cards
   - This creates visual hint that more content is available

5. **Pagination Indicators**:
   - Always include dots at bottom
   - Active dot: `w-2.5 h-2.5 bg-primary`
   - Inactive dots: `w-2 h-2 bg-muted-foreground/30`
   - Make dots clickable: `onClick={() => api?.scrollTo(index)}`

6. **Navigation Arrows**:
   - Position: `absolute left-2` and `right-2` on card edges
   - Only show when scrollable: `{canScrollPrev && ...}`
   - Style: `h-7 w-7 rounded-full bg-background/90 backdrop-blur-sm`
   - Use `ChevronLeft` and `ChevronRight` from `lucide-react`

## Visual Design Standards

### Spacing & Layout
- Base spacing unit: 4px (0.5rem = 8px, 1rem = 16px)
- Card padding: `p-3` (mobile), `p-5` (desktop)
- Gap between cards: `gap-3` (mobile), `gap-4` (desktop)
- Section spacing: `space-y-4` (mobile), `space-y-8` (desktop)

### Typography
- Headings: `font-bold`, responsive sizes (`text-sm` → `text-base`)
- Body text: `text-muted-foreground` for secondary
- Numbers: Always `tabular-nums` for alignment
- Truncation: Use `truncate` with `min-w-0` on parent container

### Colors & Theming
- Use semantic tokens: `primary`, `secondary`, `success`, `warning`, `destructive`
- APY color coding:
  - ≥15%: `text-emerald-600`
  - ≥10%: `text-emerald-500`
  - ≥5%: `text-teal-500`
  - ≥2%: `text-teal-400`
  - ≥1%: `text-cyan-500`
  - <1%: `text-muted-foreground`

### Component Styling
- Cards: `glass-card rounded-xl` class
- Borders: `border border-border` (subtle)
- Shadows: Use scale (sm, md, lg) - avoid heavy shadows
- Hover states: `hover:bg-accent`, `hover:scale-105` (subtle)

## Animation Guidelines

### Framer Motion Usage
- Import: `motion`, `AnimatePresence` from `framer-motion`
- Duration: 0.2-0.4s for most animations
- Easing: `[0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1]` (smooth, natural)
- Stagger: `delay: 0.2 + i * 0.08` for list items

### Performance
- Use `transform` and `opacity` only (GPU-accelerated)
- Avoid animating `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`
- Use `AnimatePresence` for mount/unmount animations

## Accessibility Requirements

### Interactive Elements
- All buttons/links must have `aria-label` or visible text
- Touch targets: Minimum 44x44px on mobile
- Focus states: `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring`
- Keyboard navigation: Support Tab, Enter, Arrow keys

### Screen Readers
- Use semantic HTML (`<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`)
- Add `sr-only` class for visually hidden but accessible text
- Provide context: `aria-label="Go to slide 2"` for pagination

### Color Contrast
- Text must meet WCAG AA: 4.5:1 contrast ratio
- Use `text-muted-foreground` for secondary text (lower contrast OK)
- Never rely on color alone to convey information

## Data Display Patterns

### APY/APR Formatting
- Use `formatPercent()` and `formatSpread()` from `@/lib/formatters`
- Show breakdown: `{native} + {incentive}` with `+` separator
- Incentive badges: `bg-amber-50 text-amber-600` with icon
- Always use `tabular-nums` for number alignment

### Empty States
- Show helpful message: "No {category} opportunities found"
- Center content: `text-center py-6`
- Use `text-muted-foreground` for empty state text

### Loading States
- Use skeleton loaders matching final layout
- Reference: `LoadingState.tsx` component
- Show skeletons in same grid/carousel structure as final content

## Component Patterns

### Responsive Grid
```tsx
// Desktop: 4 columns, Mobile: 2 columns
<div className="grid gap-3 md:gap-4 grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
  {/* Cards */}
</div>
```

### Mobile Carousel Wrapper
```tsx
// Desktop: Grid, Mobile: Carousel
{!isMobile ? (
  <div className="grid ...">{cards}</div>
) : (
  <Carousel>
    <CarouselContent>
      {cards.map(card => (
        <CarouselItem key={...} className="basis-[85%]">
          {card}
        </CarouselItem>
      ))}
    </CarouselContent>
    {/* Pagination & Arrows */}
  </Carousel>
)}
```

## Performance Best Practices

### Code Splitting
- Use `React.lazy()` for route-level components
- Dynamic imports for heavy dependencies

### Re-render Optimization
- Use `React.memo()` for expensive components
- Use `useMemo()` for calculated values
- Use `useCallback()` for event handlers passed as props

### Image Optimization
- Use WebP format when possible
- Add `loading="lazy"` for below-fold images
- Specify width/height to prevent layout shift

## Testing Checklist

Before submitting UI changes:
- [ ] Test on mobile viewport (< 768px)
- [ ] Test on tablet viewport (768px - 1024px)
- [ ] Test on desktop viewport (> 1024px)
- [ ] Verify carousel pagination works
- [ ] Verify navigation arrows appear/disappear correctly
- [ ] Check touch/swipe gestures on mobile
- [ ] Verify keyboard navigation
- [ ] Check color contrast ratios
- [ ] Test with screen reader (if available)
- [ ] Verify loading states match final layout
- [ ] Check empty states display correctly
